  "verbalization": "The compound [(1S,4aR,7aS)-7-hydroxy-7-methyl-1-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-4a,5,6,7a-tetrahydro-1H-cyclopenta[c]pyran-5-yl] 4-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzoate] is associated with U251 through multiple indirect pathways. It is predicted to target the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a known target of several other compounds, including (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one. This pathway suggests a potential role in proteasome regulation, which may influence cellular processes critical to U251's function. Additionally, the compound is also predicted to target Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a target of Dendridine A and Certonardosterol E3, both of which are linked to U251. These findings collectively suggest that the compound may interact with U251 through multiple molecular mechanisms, potentially involving tubulin regulation and proteasome activity. The evidence is consistent with the compound acting as a modulator of U251, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
